Yep, they're tough. Some of the methods i use to deal with ants (if i'm
not sufficiently powerful to handle them myself):

- run
- let my pet take care of them
- use elbereth and then throw things at them / zap wands
- run

If you aren't strong enough to deal with a particular monster at that
moment, then run. As a part of this, you should never be burdened as
you can't run away as fast as you'd like. Pause and think as soon as
you see an 'a' and think about how you can deal with the situation.
Don't wait for the ant to come to you, don't keep trying to attack when
all you get are misses, just take a breather and examine the situation.


Also remember, when engraving elbereth with your hands you can do it
several times to ensure that one of them will stick. Do one at a time,
and just keep adding to the engraving. Wait there until your HP is
restored, then you can do one of the other methods above to deal with
them.

Another thing you need to do is try to get your AC down as fast as you
can. Use your pet to determine which armor is cursed or not, and then
try on every piece of armor to see if it has an enchantment. Yes,
trying on every orcish helm does get tiring, but if you find a +5 one
then it will really help out. (i found a +4 small shield, and a +5
helmet last game off a random drop - rare but it happens if you try on
enough armor). Then they'll be missing _you_ all the time.

